{% endfor %}

## Pass

Every quote is a faithful paraphrase or verbatim rendering of the text at its
cited location — the SAME claim, not a nearby or related one the source
happens to also contain.

## Fail

- A quote states something the cited location does not actually say (the
  citation resolves, but to the wrong claim — a plausible-sounding
  fabrication grounded in a real-but-irrelevant location).
- A quote overstates or sharpens what the source says (the source hedges,
  the quote asserts).
- `source_text` is empty for a citation — the link resolved to a range with
  no content, which is its own kind of ungrounded.

Name the specific citation number and quote the source text it actually
diverges from.
